      "first": {
        "speaker": 0,
        "line": 3,
        "text": "“Mr Rochester. At the age of 13, Jane Eyre taught me a vital lesson about love."
      },
      "last": {
        "speaker": 0,
        "line": 769,
        "text": "So - what do you do when you build yourself - only to realise you built yourself with the wrong things? You rip it up and start again - build up and tear down, endlessly, repetitively, unceasingly. Invent invent invent! What will, eventually, be you?"
      }
